spans.s:
Nālada,
(1) v.l. in Mv 〔ii.43.2〕 for Nārada (3), q.v., referring to Nālaka; prob. the same person is meant by the sthavira Nālada Av 〔i.274.6 ff.〕;
(2) = Nālanda, birthplace of Śāriputra (Tiṣya): ˚da-grāmake Tiṣyo … (here father of Śāriputra) Av 〔ii.186.6〕 (so text, no v.l.).

nālikā,
(1) (= Pali nāḷikā), a tubular vessel or receptacle: pucchaṃ sauvarṇāyāṃ ˚kāyāṃ prakṣiptam Divy 〔514.6〕; bhaiṣajyāñjana-nālikā Mvy 〔9014〕;
(2) (= Pkt. ṇāliā, AMg. ṇālī), a metal plate on which the hour is struck: Jm 〔83.24〕.
